elastalert3 (formerly elastalert-rs) is an independent alerting daemon written
in Rust. It started as a reimplementation of the behaviour of ElastAlert 2
(https://github.com/jertel/elastalert2), Copyright Yelp and the ElastAlert 2
contributors, licensed under the Apache License 2.0, and adds features of its
own. It is not affiliated with Yelp or the ElastAlert 2 maintainers.
Rule files, configuration keys, log lines and writeback document formats are
kept compatible with ElastAlert 2 on purpose.

The documentation in docs/source is derived from the ElastAlert 2
documentation (Apache License 2.0), modified to describe elastalert3.

